WEBVTT

00:02:57.965 --> 00:03:00.509
because of how they express
their gender in public.

00:03:00.551 --> 00:03:04.305
But online Nerima could develop
many versions of themselves.

00:03:04.305 --> 00:03:05.514
For me and Nerima,

00:03:05.556 --> 00:03:08.267
the internet was the only place
where we could talk openly

00:03:08.309 --> 00:03:09.477
and support each other

00:03:09.518 --> 00:03:12.146
through some of the most difficult
moments in our lives.

00:03:12.146 --> 00:03:15.316
We helped each other and people
in our community find safe housing,

00:03:15.316 --> 00:03:16.901
navigate loss after being outed.

00:03:16.901 --> 00:03:18.069
We've hosted memorials

00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:21.364
and helped each other find
queer family experts when we needed them.

00:03:21.364 --> 00:03:24.659
These virtual networks
saved and sustained us,

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:26.994
and these experiences led
Nerima and me to create

00:03:27.036 --> 00:03:29.622
The Queer Africa Network, QAN,

00:03:29.664 --> 00:03:34.085
an online platform where we hope
to ensure that every queer African,